  "description": "Given a string s, return the number of distinct non-empty subsequences of s. Since the answer may be very large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.",
  "target": "aba",
  "pseudocode": "1. dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n2. dp[0] = 1\n3. last = {}\n4. for i from 1 to n:\n5.   dp[i] = dp[i-1] * 2\n6.   char = s[i-1]\n7.   if char in last:\n8.     dp[i] -= dp[last[char]-1]\n9.   last[char] = i\n10. return dp[n] - 1",
